codex
Run 10 revealed a second-order problem with making every non-idle test use a never-advancing clock: three socket-heavy tests can stall indefinitely when the concurrently running suite exhausts blocking I/O workers. I’m stopping this hung gate, reverting that broad clock default, and will serialize only this test suite so its blocking socket fixtures do not starve one another. The teardown race remains exercised; serialization does not replace the new completion seam.
